<title>SWEDEN: SWIMMING-SWEDEN BREAK EUROPEAN 4X100 MEDLEY RELAY RECORD.</title>
<headline>SWIMMING-SWEDEN BREAK EUROPEAN 4X100 MEDLEY RELAY RECORD.</headline>
<dateline>GOTHENBURG, Sweden 1997-04-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sweden set a European women's 4x100 metres medley relay short-course record at the world short-course swimming championships on Sunday.</p>
<p>Therese Alshammar, Hanna Jaltner, Johanna Sjoberg and Malin Svahnstrom finished fourth in four minutes 2.42 seconds to beat the 4:02.85 mark set by an East German quartet in Indianapolis on January 8, 1983.</p>
</text>
